# The entrypoint is read by the Linux kernel's shebang handling inside the container. A
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would give it CRLF endings, and the container would
# fail to start with "exec /app/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" - the
# kernel having tried to run "/bin/sh\r". The Dockerfile strips CRs as well; this stops
# them existing in the first place.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else a Linux container parses. nginx.conf picked up CRLF on
# the commit that added it, which is how this was noticed: the file is read by nginx
# inside the image, and a config it half-understands is a worse failure than one it
# rejects outright.
*.conf text eol=lf
